# Test-only credentials template for E2E runs against a real Supabase backend.
# Copy to .env.test and fill in your values. Never commit .env.test.
#
# These are read at the Node layer, by the Playwright step definitions
# (tests/e2e/steps/auth_setup.ts, `process.env.TEST_*`), and never by the app:
# no VITE_ prefix, so Vite never inlines them into the client bundle.
# The mock client (VITE_USE_MOCK_SUPABASE=true) needs none of them: it accepts
# its own fixed demo password, test-password-123 (frontend/src/lib/mockSupabaseClient.js).
# Playwright's web server always runs the mock (playwright.config.ts), so these
# apply only to a run against a real backend; don't export TEST_PASSWORD for a
# mock run, where the UI sign-in step types it.
TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
TEST_COACH_EMAIL=coach@example.com
TEST_PARENT_EMAIL=parent@example.com
TEST_PASSWORD=
